// dsv4-validate-run.bml -- the physical validation window of the Form-native DeepSeek-V4 driver. ONE window, ALONE, on the IQ2XXS file, staged so the machine is read at every step.
//
//   echo '{"dry":1}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-validate-run.bml      the plan: what the window WILL do, the lease, the stages and their asks, the abort rules, the references, what the driver cannot run yet.
//                                                                 Reads the file's header window, the machine and the process list (the organs of ours resident, by name); opens nothing, maps nothing, takes no lease, writes no row.
//                                                                 Empty stdin and {} do the same: THE DEFAULT IS THE PLAN.
//   echo '{"go":1}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-validate-run.bml       THE WINDOW. Not run by the session that wrote it: it asks for the lead's go. While the header names tensors the driver cannot run, it
//                                                                 maps nothing: it writes a receipt row naming them and stops.
//
// stdin, one JSON line, all optional: go (1 runs the window; anything else prints the plan), dry (1 forces the plan even with go), file (the GGUF; the IQ2XXS build by default), cap (position capacity, 64), cache_experts (the lease's expert cache a layer, 64), arena_slots (experts a layer's arena holds, 64: the routed stacks are not mapped and a missing expert is filled by span; 0 maps the stacks whole, the control),
// logits_prompt_ids (replaces the recorded logits' 14 chat-templated prompt ids, which the row form/form-stdlib/tests/oracles/ds4-logits-capital-of-france-prompt.json pins; the leg waits only when neither holds), receipt (the row's file, receipts/dsv4-validation.jsonl).
//
// Before it starts the window checks, and refuses on any: no other model door resident (the process rows flp-gpu-holders reads, a ds4 process, another copy of this door), no lease another process holds, the
// machine not low, the recorded logits file the pinned one (SHA-256), the file a deepseek4 GGUF with a consistent layout, and the governor granting the window's lease (derived working set, not file_size).
// Every rule, estimate and the run itself are definitions of form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-validate.bml, read there and held by its band. Exit: 0 for a completed window with every handle released, 1 otherwise.
// Inside the window a stage's ask denied for reserve or compressor backs off (10 s doubling to 60 s, 5 minutes an ask at most) before the run ends, and the receipt carries the reading that denied (denied, vm_window)
// and the organs of ours resident (organs, moved). The layers are not staged here: observe/dsv4-token-run.bml measures the token path as it runs.
// Check the machine first: ./fkwu observe/memory-governor-run.bml </dev/null must show no leases and room; run nothing else against the GPU while the window is open.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-validate.bml
section [form.bml] {
 dvr-main();
}
